==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Siege Walker Diabolosa''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Obliterator Diabolosa''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
What stands out is that range and damage are both excellent, especially against the traits it targets, making for an excellent [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Anti Angel]] attacker, more than anything; one of the best, stat-wise. Use it in tandem with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and Angels will fall like nothing. Its high health makes it effective in presence of [[Sunfish Jones]], while its range lets it stay safe from even [[St. Dober]], resulting in a good matchup almost every time! The only Angels that may trouble this unit are those with waves/long range and high damage, or [[Heavenly Herald Papuu|Papuu]]'s toxic attacks.

Against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], Diabolosa is not as effective due to the slow-ish attacks and zombies' tendency to pop up anywhere and start attacking, but the health tends to offer good enough survivability from such ambushes. The only real issue comes in the concrete possibility of remaining isolated, meaning that it is best not to send it out too early. With some care, however, its health, damage and range will often result in this unit surviving for very long and making a difference in a fight.

The long range and high health also make this unit excellent against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Akus]], as it can often avoid being hit by [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Death Surges]] and tank the damage if it can't avoid them. It might lack Shield Piercing, but it more than makes up for it with its high DPS, resulting in this unit being very effective against almost every Aku enemy introduced thus far, including [[Dark Priest Mamon|both]] [[High Priest Mamon|Mamon]]'s encounters and [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Jagando's stage]]. If the units in charge of protecting it fail to do so effectively, however, know that it may die early and never come back in time, so investing in its protection is a must. Shield Piercers are still recommended to use alongside this unit, so that it may get the most of its damage by striking Aku enemies down without wasting time on breaking shields.

==='''True Form'''===
Nothing big changes when it comes to usage, it just becomes better, but there are some new doors that open: Immunity to freeze helps when this unit gets ambushed by a [[Zir Zeal]] or when fighting [[Wicked Face]], not to mention making this unit available in stages with [[Henry]] and few other specific situations, while the greatly improved damage makes this unit a considerably more reliable backline attacker.

Aside from the stat buffs and immunities, this unit gains a good attack combo with Manic Flying Cat, which is identical to [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] but takes only two slots instead of four, making this evolution worth the Catfruit even for just the combo. Manic Flying Cat is also part of the [[Aerial Recon (Combo)|Aerial Recon]] and the [[Saucers (Combo)|Saucers]] combos. So, you can get Medium Attack UP, Medium Research UP, and Small "Massive Damage" effect UP simultaneously, which can provide an extremely strong boost in certain stages.

==='''Talents'''===
Obliterator Diabolosa's wide slew of Talents are generally beneficial, and will usually be worth the investment in the long run.

As Diabolosa is primarily used for its damage, '''HP Buff''' isn't of much importance. '''Attack Buff''' could potentially prove useful to increase its damage output, though in either case players should prioritize investing [[Catseye]]s, as both are very expensive for what they do.

'''[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]''' is perhaps of top priority, as it addresses one of the unit's most significant drawbacks against Aku threats by simply dismissing every Surge they spawn while continuing to provide DPS. This also extends to Surge-heavy stages in general if they feature threats within its target traits, as while Zombies are not known to abuse Surges ([[Lophiiformes Angaburu]]'s Mini-Surges are very weak), the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] can be quite the threat, as is [[St. Dober]]/[[Mini Angel Cyclone]], or just about any enemy that [[Surge Attack#Counter-Surge|Counter]] any Surges hitting them.

'''[[Colossus Slayer]]''' is also worth mentioning. Granted, Diabolosa isn't a great generalist, so this limits it to the few compatible threats within its targeted traits. Naturally, while it is unable to evade [[Big Peng Z]]'s nasty 50% Toxic attacks (its Omni Strikes reach up to 500 range), it does fully outrange [[Archangel Exiel]] (Omni Strike reaches up to 260). In the case of [[Omens]], Diabolosa also outranges it (430<475), and its vulnerability to their Surges can be simply patched with the relevant talent, again making it an excellent counter when given the right support. Otherwise, it can provide supplementary DPS against Colossus threats outside of its targeted traits if it happens to be useful against supporting threats.

'''[[Soulstrike]]''' is somewhat questionable. As with [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Tigerclaw]], Diabolosa moves very slowly, has a sluggish attack animation, and targeting fallen Zombie peons would simply waste its powerful attacks, even if they occur somewhat frequently, making it situational at best.

Finally, '''[[Immune to Knockback|Knockback Immunity]]''' is rather detrimental, simply because Diabolosa has only three knockbacks, and this hinders the unit's ability to reposition.

==='''Orb'''===
As Diabolosa targets three traits, players should feel free to equip a Massive Damage Orb corresponding to whichever trait they are used against the most.

